CORE gcc-only
main.i
--arch x86_64
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line 24 plain read-modify-write: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line 25 locked increment: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
approximating inline assembly
--
A lock-prefixed instruction is an atomic section on its own: making the whole
statement atomic would hide the race on the plain read-modify-write of x.
